 all a surprisingly fun drop!","caption":"Chestnut Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/252862","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/252862"}},{"id":"252899","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"252900","description":"The right line at around 250-300cfs.  \r\n\r\nIt's a little tough to get lined up due to the lack of features leading to the drop, but the water is slack enough at this level to give you plenty of time to adjust.  The slot at the top gets tight at the bottom and ends with a hole that doesn't look all that friendly.  The rapid is blasted so the rock is a tad on the sharp side.  All in all a surprisingly fun drop!","caption":"Chestnut Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/252899","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/252899"}},{"id":"872540","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872541","description":"","caption":"Is that Aaron, Roger, John or Eric","poi_name":"Camera","subject":"","author":"Connie Harmon","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872540","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872540"}},{"id":"872550","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872551","description":"Jeff, sizing up his line.","caption":"Jeff Allen","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872550","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872550"}},{"id":"872570","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872571","description":"Ice floes on the New River in March after they had broken up and melted.","caption":"Dixie on Ice","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872570","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872570"}}],"detail":{"id":"1915","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"William Gilbert wrote, in Nov. 2000:\n\nChestnut is a nice creek to run -- beginners can run it with no problems. If you make the run down to the river then you will have to get out and scout one fall (Chestnut Falls); its about an 8-ft drop. Run river right and you will flow down a chute. When the water is up you can go a few diferent ways, but only rarely does the water get that high\n\nMay everyone have a safe float,\n\nWilliam Gilbert [scvgilbert@hotmail.com](mailto:scvgilbert@hotmail.com)\n\nslide show from 10/04/15 run of last 2.5 miles (793 to Byllesby boat ramp), featuring SUP\n\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rlg4vVu9hlc](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rlg4vVu9hlc)  (7 min)\n\nSee Also:\n\n_Classic Virginia Rivers,_ Ed Grove (1992 ed), p. 294.\n\n_Virginia Whitewater_, Roger Corbett (2000 ed.), p. 449.\n\n_Exploring Virginia's Waterways_, Ed Gertler (2022 ed.), p. 328.","averageGradient":"13","maxGradient":"20","length":"13","correlations":[{"reachID":"1915","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"200","beginMediumRunnable":"480","beginHighRunnable":"600","endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"CHESTNUT CREEK AT GALAX, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03165000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"33","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.36","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.